# Implementation Plan - Peacock OS Window Controls, Battery Fix & Chrome Integration

Fix window minimize/close controls across all windows, resolve battery percentage rounding/desktop detection/periodical sync issues, and integrate Google Chrome search functionality into the Peacock OS taskbar.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Window Titlebars**: All frameless windows in Peacock OS will now render a unified draggable `#window-titlebar` with standard minimize (`─`) and close (`✕`) buttons wired to IPC window controls.
> - **Battery Broadcasting**: All system components (Taskbar, Control Panel, Settings) will subscribe to a single 30-second periodic IPC broadcast from `lexer.py` to prevent battery percentage drift across app windows.
> - **Chrome & Search Integration**: A 🔍 Search button will be added to the taskbar. Web searches use `shell.openExternal`. If Chrome is not found at standard installation paths, an alert prompt will inform the user with a download link while safely using the system default browser.

